#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124194 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e593685-f5ca-5501-94bf-7cb4d49e935b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals"}] :question/id #uuid "a2c947c7-9873-5137-91ca-4fe0b42e9bb7" :question/math-academy-id "e-11021" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](images/5b/5b534c95f0105645223836a1b44f38db3f14bf61425b6f53ee7815742a86a068.svg)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124195 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4fd256-a726-523c-84dc-f62d4e2711cc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Domain of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "42cbeba7-685e-5782-9695-9671d16b7f80" :question/math-academy-id "e-11022" :question/problem "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](images/68/68197b31685c209b98416f8e137dca514d7fbbf382d400688d411fa633ffd3c0.svg)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\, : \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain. \n\n- Starting with $y> -x,$ we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/6a/6aa1aaeadb177cf5a80bcb12a247725cb3396586e7516c3ba30b46b03a9d2612.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124196 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9289c4d-4f7f-5704-a2cb-272f92d8fef3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Two-Variable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "59fa0287-0562-5cf2-8469-946a69dc8adf" :question/math-academy-id "e-11025" :question/problem "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124198 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f2bc84-03e8-5921-81e2-683a09195279" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Containing Exponential, Logarithmic, and Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "bdae9fe0-a491-531b-ac36-7a37d2c32f16" :question/math-academy-id "e-11029" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y>0 \\\\ x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e593685-f5ca-5501-94bf-7cb4d49e935b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00bacbcd-590d-557f-a9f4-6a4269e68310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272390} {:answer/id #uuid "8f76b85c-0fb2-5e25-b12d-307a72a16bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273631} {:answer/id #uuid "df3e244c-ae04-56cb-8d2f-103fe2a767ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274357} {:answer/id #uuid "e6619d40-8fda-56f8-ab78-d3db56de9c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274424} {:answer/id #uuid "fe29f23c-2a64-564f-9465-5e972cf08268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe29f23c-2a64-564f-9465-5e972cf08268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274622} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d3ee636-ed6b-5d29-ac3b-8e818ea5617f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8022d60c-ad02-52ea-a2bc-6bcc108f5f02" :question/math-academy-id "q-158179" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4fd256-a726-523c-84dc-f62d4e2711cc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Domain of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7dd88c6-a262-58f6-95e2-e5384e5a31d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/18/18dcabdd46f686f12ce0577d5398b525976ee8404209d24a187c3d372a3bf78a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378748} {:answer/id #uuid "e43659e6-8eca-521f-a3ac-7988fc36588b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c4add22572db01658a9c909f66be2d53f14331454ab32577ced33011fe05fafa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378749} {:answer/id #uuid "50b317ce-e6eb-5c10-bf7a-1fcf5464941b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c641990be320fa60b602e3d42ab5d29648eb3d5274645f8193018d132c964599.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378750} {:answer/id #uuid "04ab281c-1447-5ea1-a446-2b1264179bd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e79d4b0590032bc951f56e3117a6e5048e7101e270043b3e01b11e961b8c52a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378751} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2d7682-8df8-5624-9a62-ae12d475ff4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e646fe749cc50c557df1a35c69d9de75b16064afe42e467e62784b705c189b36.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b2d7682-8df8-5624-9a62-ae12d475ff4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e646fe749cc50c557df1a35c69d9de75b16064afe42e467e62784b705c189b36.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378752} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0adcc51-cdb5-5e33-a2ed-45fc79d72d4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f8af9ca-3fa0-5528-bb2b-5f736d2c06fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-158204" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{y+{x}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\ny+{x}^{2}\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,y\\ge -{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $\\ge $ sign, the curve is part of the domain. Therefore, we draw a solid curve $y=-{x}^{2}$ and shade the area *outside* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/0b/0b7a6dbbab890b469cf389fa27627e9c1a5f95d8892507fcd4ba5f70541936ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9289c4d-4f7f-5704-a2cb-272f92d8fef3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Two-Variable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d569954b-a9bd-5e60-8d8d-dc21240f8373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121422} {:answer/id #uuid "31ab3514-afb9-55f0-b797-5d67fafbd447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121423} {:answer/id #uuid "50456efb-8153-58c0-b558-6f6aca1e4608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121424} {:answer/id #uuid "55fccb26-6f80-5c7f-a2da-3df8bb2dc868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121425} {:answer/id #uuid "69feff14-68ef-55b8-89be-19860c1c8bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121426}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5c3de9-0c28-55d6-a0e6-dcc003a6afdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121421}] :question/id #uuid "15761064-db02-546d-ba8e-469a8fb53fd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-158245" :question/problem "Evaluate $z = x^{2} + xy - 5$ at the point $(1, 2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e593685-f5ca-5501-94bf-7cb4d49e935b" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd264dd-57f7-5f83-8438-70da99d972ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276194} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc00d9a-8c46-5e1f-b5b7-46d57f9146e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne -1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276334} {:answer/id #uuid "697714b4-389d-552a-afd9-dfeb9508cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276424} {:answer/id #uuid "9eae026c-0425-5d9d-9d0d-2c5cc016d5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy-$plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276902} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cbb466-1959-5593-a863-cfdf8e0a86fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd264dd-57f7-5f83-8438-70da99d972ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276194} :answer-field/id #uuid "df108a95-6e90-54f8-bc6b-d51e2e24412d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83b99b1c-0bfd-5266-a9a8-e11b90bb0b2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158553" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{2x+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2x+y\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne 0}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9289c4d-4f7f-5704-a2cb-272f92d8fef3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Two-Variable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c76e3aa-4667-51f4-960b-54ca94e95bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276006} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9d4847-f4a3-5e51-8843-844c295abf04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276161} {:answer/id #uuid "547dc3c1-d89d-5b16-897a-edc2f16a48c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276228} {:answer/id #uuid "56bc4319-f696-511e-8032-dbec796ecaea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276251} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d39fd4-0a44-568e-b95b-3b8fe25d4342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c76e3aa-4667-51f4-960b-54ca94e95bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276006} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4ad22a6-5ade-5693-8d0f-ccaadfcf6954" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f50b49cb-5ece-5d2a-8bc6-eb00c81b1f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-158572" :question/problem "Evaluate $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2y+4)$ at the point $(-4,1).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-4,1),$ we substitute $x=-4$ and $y=1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(-4,1)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2y+4)\\,{|}_{(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3(-4)-2(1)+4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-12-2+4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-10),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f2bc84-03e8-5921-81e2-683a09195279" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Function Containing Exponential, Logarithmic, and Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fbc55dd-d8d2-5b43-b11f-9a50efe89dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275904} {:answer/id #uuid "3183d17e-b7c4-54e7-b556-7307de6fccdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275917} {:answer/id #uuid "4236b259-5922-523f-b30b-035b4ffb366e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276056} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd8d44b-46d1-5eb0-b119-0f85bfe1eab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 0,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276336} {:answer/id #uuid "6f7a5bbc-3365-5bba-82b2-9e07c2d95446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fbc55dd-d8d2-5b43-b11f-9a50efe89dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275904} :answer-field/id #uuid "123bde27-b22e-5118-aaaf-2bd06d63606a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "806bcc75-b225-5d86-8c9e-f99567365362" :question/math-academy-id "q-158577" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4fd256-a726-523c-84dc-f62d4e2711cc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Domain of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31993f67-cb13-54c1-825f-a871eb2dd965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/044cb99eef6bafea63a4b4dd8df2a465790ea8eda949d98dd97df2ed768791be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378831} {:answer/id #uuid "6e60753e-9691-518b-a34b-cefcf9d4bc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/934de8df0f2c2a0c93d3966a66f1eed69744079f4beee57d7cc46e6ca20fddcb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378832} {:answer/id #uuid "7ade9180-8b54-5d3a-bfdb-c1cb7778c73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2ddf4edfd91b14835e7b14ca8cebf08b82b8585d9fd18972c8b065d6153a62f0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378833} {:answer/id #uuid "501346e1-a1e0-553c-96ce-2d555eb1295a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/280ac039d18c0af132b0a2a85a3b94226c7ff2b310c460a1086d52402bc41865.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378834} {:answer/id #uuid "9eae9821-d4e8-5aa2-84b4-d170a1a95d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a111de19f5b6fdc447cac043e875b243c67709180ca23b2283d448cdbfda94d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31993f67-cb13-54c1-825f-a871eb2dd965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/044cb99eef6bafea63a4b4dd8df2a465790ea8eda949d98dd97df2ed768791be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378831} :answer-field/id #uuid "04cdf5f5-74c6-51ca-8422-d1cd0d51b9e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56f9c6d4-908f-5999-9300-6cd67e4208c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-158600" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+y\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,y\\ne -{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ne -{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the line is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ and shade *above* and *below* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/6c/6c85783dc6626a3fea9d06431ee31e202da8c4d88e2eb1c2b6608dccdc2b782e.png)"}]}
